Task 2: Set Up Message Queue and Routing
Subtask 2.1: Create Camel Route
Create src/main/java/com/example/ActiveMQRoutes.java:

import org.apache.camel.builder.RouteBuilder;

public class ActiveMQRoutes extends RouteBuilder {
    @Override
    public void configure() throws Exception {
        // Route to consume from ActiveMQ queue
        from("activemq:queue:inputQueue")
            .log("Received message: ${body}")
            .process(exchange -> {
                String message = exchange.getIn().getBody(String.class);
                String processedMsg = "Processed: " + message;
                exchange.getMessage().setBody(processedMsg);
            })
            .to("activemq:queue:outputQueue");
    }
}
Subtask 2.2: Create Main Application Class
Create src/main/java/com/example/ActiveMQDemo.java:

import org.apache.camel.main.Main;
import org.apache.camel.component.activemq.ActiveMQComponent;

public class ActiveMQDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Main main = new Main();
        
        // Configure ActiveMQ component
        ActiveMQComponent activemq = new ActiveMQComponent();
        activemq.setBrokerURL("tcp://localhost:61616");
        activemq.setUsername("admin");
        activemq.setPassword("admin");
        
        main.bind("activemq", activemq);
        main.addRouteBuilder(new ActiveMQRoutes());
        
        System.out.println("Starting Camel. Press CTRL+C to terminate.");
        main.run();
    }
}
Task 3: Implement Transactional Processing
Subtask 3.1: Modify Route for Transactions
Update ActiveMQRoutes.java:

from("activemq:queue:inputQueue?transacted=true")
    .transacted()
    .log("Received message: ${body}")
    .process(exchange -> {
        String message = exchange.getIn().getBody(String.class);
        if(message.contains("error")) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Simulated error");
        }
        String processedMsg = "Processed: " + message;
        exchange.getMessage().setBody(processedMsg);
    })
    .to("activemq:queue:outputQueue")
    .log("Message processed successfully");
Subtask 3.2: Test Transactional Behavior
Run the application:
mvn compile exec:java -Dexec.mainClass="com.example.ActiveMQDemo"
Send test messages using ActiveMQ web console:
Send a normal message (should process successfully)
Send a message containing "error" (should trigger rollback)
Verification Steps
Check ActiveMQ admin console (http://localhost:8161/admin):

Verify messages are in the correct queues
Check DLQ (Dead Letter Queue) for failed messages
Expected outcomes:

Normal messages appear in outputQueue
Messages with "error" remain in inputQueue (due to rollback)
System logs show processing attempts
Troubleshooting Tips
If ActiveMQ connection fails:

Verify ActiveMQ is running (netstat -tulnp | grep 61616)
Check credentials in application.properties
If messages aren't processing:

Check Camel logs for errors
Verify queue names match in producer and consumer
For transaction issues:

Ensure transacted=true is set in the endpoint URI
Check ActiveMQ transaction logs
